Done. The plugin's browser half now truly activates, verified in a real browser.

## Root cause

`window.__ModuleLoader__` keys each boot-graph row by the **resolved package name**, and after fetching a row's bundle it asserts that exact id was registered:

```
client-modules: bundle <url> loaded without registering "<id>" via __ModuleLoader__.load
```

`/app/fixture/client.js` registered its factory under the stale id `@demo/dsh-bench-browser-activation-legacy`. Everything else was healthy (host row, manifest entry in `window.__DSH_BOOT__.entries`, HTTP 200 on `/plugins/...client.js`), so the loader loaded the script but never found the factory for `@demo/dsh-bench-browser-activation` — hence no activation and no marker.

## Fix

`/app/fixture/client.js` — registration id changed to the package name (misleading comment corrected). No other fixture file touched.

```js
window.__ModuleLoader__.load({
  id: '@demo/dsh-bench-browser-activation',
  ...
})
```

## Verification (isolated profile, real Chromium)

- Used a throwaway `DSH_HOME=/tmp/dsh-verify-home` and profile `verify` (bundles: `dsh-base`, `dsh-web-app`, the fixture); the host profile `/root/.dsh/profiles/migrate` was untouched.
- Booted `dsh --profile verify --no-open --port 0` (0.1.2-alpha.2) and drove the tokenized URL with Chromium 154 + playwright-core (`--single-process --no-zygote --disable-crashpad-for-testing` were needed only because this container's sandbox breaks Chromium's zygote/crashpad).
- **Positive result**: `document.documentElement.dataset.benchBrowserActivation === "active"`, the row is in `__DSH_BOOT__.entries`, the served bundle text registers exactly `@demo/dsh-bench-browser-activation` (no `-legacy`), HTTP 200, zero console/page errors.
- **Negative control** with the pre-fix bundle reproduced the reported failure: marker absent and `failed to import loader entry ... loaded without registering "@demo/dsh-bench-browser-activation"`.

Cleanup: Chromium crash-probe `core.<pid>` dumps left in `/app` were deleted (only `fixture/client.js` is modified), test servers stopped, and an evidence report was written to `/app/agent-output/H10-verification.md`.

